    livianapf_architecture_lead: 'And now the part I find most interesting myself: something genuinely simple that can be built in a matter of hours.',
    livianapf_challenge_intro: 'Offering a language model publicly and without a sign in also means that every click can cost money. For a demo I did not want the running cost of a web application firewall.',
    livianapf_challenge_layers: 'So I built the protection myself: the throttling in API Gateway, a limit per session, a daily cap, reserved concurrency and a limit on message length.',
    livianapf_challenge_outro: 'What mattered most here was the order of the checks. Expensive requests are allowed through as late as possible, and a rejected request uses up none of the daily allowance.',
    livianapf_result_1: 'Liviana has been running on kettenki.com since August 2026, answers in three to five seconds and switches language automatically.',
    livianapf_result_2: 'The most important thing I took away is that with a public chatbot the prompt is only a small part of the work. It gets more interesting with the things that can go wrong: too many requests, a service that has failed, a daily limit that has been reached, or an attempt to pull the chatbot out of its role.',
